<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.75%" pitch="-2.60%">
            The disciples look at what they have.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            "We have only five loaves here," they say.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            "And two fish."
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            In another Gospel we are told these belonged to a boy.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            A child who had brought a small lunch.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Five small loaves of barley bread.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Two fish.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            It is not a meal.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            It is barely a snack for one person.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            And facing them is a crowd of five thousand men,
            <break time="500ms"/>
            plus women and children.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            The number is beyond counting in any practical sense.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            The gap between what they have
            <break time="500ms"/>
            and what the crowd needs
            <break time="500ms"/>
            is so large it does not even seem worth naming.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            And yet they name it.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They bring what they have to Jesus.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            That small act matters.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They do not hide the five loaves and say nothing.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They do not walk away because it is not enough.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            They say what they have.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They offer it.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            And that is where the miracle begins.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            With the small offering.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            With the honest admission of not enough.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Placed in the hands of Jesus.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
